UNIT check_carried
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/sir/v05.mjs checkCarried(decl, table), with canonical(t) and canonicalValue(t) — the carried-data gate; the code is the truth, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG check_carried(decl: json, table: json) -> record[sha: text, hashOk: bool | none, results: list[record[expr: text, equals: bool | f64 | text | list[json] | map[text, json] | none, got: bool | f64 | text | list[json] | map[text, json] | none, ok: bool]], attested: bool, status: text, entries: i64]
ENVELOPE decl is any json value and table is any json value; every map key and text is well-formed Unicode; a table or
  an equals may hold NaN, an infinity or -0 at any depth. Every malformed input is IN scope as a throw (R1). Map key ORDER
  never matters (R2, R5).
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Check a bound carried table against its declaration: hash the table's canonical form, compare the hash with
  the declared pin, evaluate each AUTHORITY assertion (the entry count, or one entry looked up by key) against its
  expected value in the canonical form, and classify the table as unpinned, hash-mismatch, unattested, attested or
  authority-FAIL. decl is the declaration map: sha (the declared pin, optional) and assertions (a list of maps, each expr
  and equals). The result record is, in this order: sha (the computed hash), hashOk, results (one record per assertion,
  in order), attested, status, entries.
BEHAVIOR
R1 Each of these throws, and a call that throws produces no result (which one is reported is not graded): decl is not a
  map (none, text, a number, a bool, a list); decl has no assertions entry or its assertions is not a list (none, text and
  a map included); decl has a sha entry that is PRESENT (R3) and not a PIN; table is not a map (a list, text, a number, a
  bool, none); table has no CANON (R2); an element of assertions, wherever it stands in the list, is not a map, or lacks
  an expr entry, or has an expr that is not text or is the empty text, or lacks an equals entry; an element's equals has
  no CANON. equals none is well-formed; any non-empty expr is well-formed, blank or invisible text (" ", U+200B) included.
R2 CANON of a json value is compact JSON with no whitespace: a map is "{" then its entries joined by "," then "}", each
  entry the key as a JSON STRING, ":", and the value's CANON, the entries ordered by key ascending, keys compared as
  sequences of UTF-16 code units, at EVERY depth; a list is "[" then its elements' CANON joined by "," then "]", in list
  order; text is a JSON STRING; true, false and none are the texts "true", "false" and "null"; a number is NUMBER-TEXT;
  NaN, the infinities and negative zero have NO CANON, nor does any value containing one. sha is the SHA-256 digest
  (FIPS 180-4) of the UTF-8 bytes of the table's CANON, written as 64 lowercase hex digits.
R3 Let S be decl's sha entry. S is ABSENT when decl has no sha entry or S is none; otherwise it is PRESENT, and a PRESENT S
  must be a PIN — text of exactly 64 characters, each one of 0-9 or a-f — or the call throws (R1: uppercase hex of the
  right digest, 63 or 65 digits, a trailing newline or space, the empty text, a bool, a number, a list, a map). hashOk is
  none when S is ABSENT, and otherwise true exactly when S equals sha.
R4 For each assertion A, in order, GOT is: when A's expr is exactly the text "count", the number of entries of the table —
  even when the table has its own entry named count, which is never read this way CITED FIDELITY package. Otherwise,
  when the table has an entry keyed by A's expr (any key: __proto__, constructor, toString and the empty text included),
  GOT is that entry's value; otherwise GOT is ABSENT. Only the table's own entries exist — no key is ever inherited.
R5 ok is true exactly when GOT is not ABSENT and CANON(GOT) is the same text as CANON(E), E being A's equals (which has a
  CANON, R1). Equivalently: GOT and E are the same json value — maps by key set and value per key with entry order
  ignored, lists element by element in order, numbers by value (7 and 7.0 are one number), text by content. An ABSENT
  GOT fails whatever E is, none included.
R6 Each result record is exactly: expr = A's expr; equals = A's equals; got = GOT (none when ABSENT); ok per R5 — A's other
  entries (its own got, ok or anything else) are dropped. attested is true exactly when hashOk is true, assertions is
  non-empty and every ok is true. entries = the number of entries of the table.
TABLE STATUS — the first matching row
  hashOk is none               | unpinned
  hashOk is false              | hash-mismatch
  assertions is empty          | unattested
  attested is true             | attested
  otherwise                    | authority-FAIL
PINNED grammar JSON-STRING = a double quote, each character of the text by ESCAPE, a double quote CITED R2 — the host's JSON string writer
TABLE ESCAPE — one character of a text inside a JSON STRING
  double quote (U+0022)                                   | backslash, double quote
  backslash (U+005C)                                      | two backslashes
  U+0008 / U+0009 / U+000A / U+000C / U+000D              | backslash then b / t / n / f / r
  any other character U+0000 to U+001F                    | backslash, u, then 4 LOWERCASE hex digits of the code point
  every other character (U+007F, U+2028, U+2029, slash, non-ASCII, supplementary) | itself, UTF-8 encoded in the hashed bytes
PINNED grammar NUMBER-TEXT = the host's shortest round-trip decimal of a finite double CITED R2 — Number::toString
  0 is "0". Otherwise a leading "-" when negative, then with digits d1..dk the SHORTEST that read back as the same double
  (k minimal; the nearest such digit string) and n such that the value is 0.d1..dk times 10^n: when k <= n <= 21, the
  digits then n - k zeros (1e20 is "100000000000000000000"); when 0 < n <= 21, the digits with "." after the n-th; when
  -6 < n <= 0, "0." then -n zeros then the digits (0.000001 is "0.000001"); otherwise exponent form: d1, then "." and
  d2..dk when k > 1, then "e", then "+" or "-", then the decimal of |n - 1| (1e21 is "1e+21", 1e-7 is "1e-7", 1.5e-7 is
  "1.5e-7", 5e-324 is "5e-324").
INVARIANT entries is the GOT of every count assertion; attested implies hashOk is true and status attested; status is
  unpinned exactly when hashOk is none, exactly when S is ABSENT; neither argument is modified.
ORACLE value -> oracles/check_carried.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 1c0a195a32524eb102837628ee60a8554ae88f742e3736aa261ddfa00e838dc4
SCOPE IN: R1–R6 over ENVELOPE, the five statuses, the refusals (R1) and the PIN form (R3), count shadowing, own-key lookup
  (__proto__ and the inherited member names ABSENT), order-free map comparison. OUT: every
  caller — carriedDeclared (which builds decl from SIR text) and carriedTable (which reads a bound module) are other units.
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 (rederive, MIT) cli/sir/v05.mjs: checkCarried, canonical, canonicalValue, plainMap,
  sha256. Re-cut 2026-10-27 (round 5), delta re-cut round 5b (FINDINGS #108) for REDERIVE_SELF_PLAN Tier 3 from the pinned authority snapshot only; oracle
  stamped by selfhost/stamp.mjs through seams/check_carried.mjs.
